# Project: Universal Accounting Learning & Practice Platform

You are working on a bilingual (English/French, later Pidgin) accounting
learning-and-practice web platform. Read PROGRESS_LOG.md before starting any
task — it tells you exactly what session we're on and what already exists.
Never assume; check the actual files on disk before writing code.

## Non-negotiable rules for every session

- Stack: React + Tailwind CSS (frontend), FastAPI + Pydantic + SQLAlchemy or
  SQLModel + Alembic (backend), PostgreSQL (database).
- The accounting engine must be deterministic. No AI-based logic decides a
  debit/credit outcome. That is out of scope entirely for now.
- OHADA and IFRS are separate, configurable "framework" contexts. Never merge
  them into one generic chart of accounts. Never generate an "official"
  OHADA chart of accounts from memory or training data — use a small,
  clearly-labeled ILLUSTRATIVE/DEMO chart of accounts only, and say so in
  code comments and seed data.
- Every posted double-entry transaction must balance: total debits = total
  credits. Enforce this at the database/service layer, not only in the UI.
- Posted records are immutable or corrected via reversing entries — never
  silently edited or deleted.
- Currency: default XAF/FCFA, zero decimal places, but store currency and
  precision as explicit configurable fields, not hard-coded assumptions.
- Every backend change to accounting logic needs an automated test written
  in the same session — do not defer testing to later.
- Keep services separated and independently testable: transaction_service,
  posting_service, ledger_service, trial_balance_service,
  financial_statement_service, account_service, framework_service.
- Repository layout: frontend/src/{components,pages,layouts,features,
  services,hooks,i18n,utils}, backend/app/{api,core,models,schemas,services,
  repositories,accounting,learning,tests}, backend/alembic/, docs/, scripts/,
  .env.example, README.md.
- UI must be usable on a phone-width browser from the start. This is a
  responsive web app, NOT a native mobile app.
- Store English/French strings separately from application logic (i18n
  folder), even before full translation content exists.

## Working style

- Only work on the session I explicitly tell you to work on. Do not jump
  ahead to future sessions even if it seems efficient.
- Before writing code, briefly restate your plan for the session and wait
  for me to confirm, unless I've told you to proceed directly.
- At the end of every session, update PROGRESS_LOG.md yourself: add a new
  entry with the date, session number, what was built, what decisions were
  made, and what the next session should do. This is the most important
  step — do not skip it even if I forget to ask.
- If you hit a rate limit or get cut off mid-task, the next thing that
  happens (even in a new chat, even with a different model) should be able
  to read PROGRESS_LOG.md and continue correctly. Write the log entry with
  that in mind.